# In-body comment ban (scripts/comments.py, `just comments`): a comment is a doc
# comment stating its item's contract. Every other comment, trailing ones
# included, is banned, except a lone one-line `// SAFETY: ...` or ADR pointer
# (`// ADR-0051 §3`, nothing after it). Each entry below is a file that already held banned
# comment lines, with their count when it was listed: it may shrink, never grow.
# `just comments-update` lowers an entry when its file sheds comments and removes
# it at 0; no entry is ever raised or added. The /delete-comment skill sweeps a
# crate.
limit 0
test-limit 0
